{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HiQS-Labs/Needle-fork/pulls/10","id":4476353215,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUQg_3c8AAAABCs-6vw","html_url":"https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/Needle-fork/pull/10","diff_url":"https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/Needle-fork/pull/10.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/Needle-fork/pull/10.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HiQS-Labs/Needle-fork/issues/10","number":10,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"SOP Steps 2/4/5: operational rails from LESSONS-LEARNED (stacked on #6)","user":{"login":"noelsaw1","id":56978803,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2OTc4ODAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56978803?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1","html_url":"https://github.com/noelsaw1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Stacked on #6** — branched off `governance/issue-is-sot` so it carries §5.7 and cannot conflict with that PR, which is still open and also edits `SOP.md`. **Merge after #6.** The diff against `main` will include #6's changes until that lands.\n\nPromotes **three** of the ten entries in `LESSONS-LEARNED.md` into SOP. The other seven stay put deliberately: they are judgment, not procedure, and importing all ten would turn SOP into a second lessons file until the two documents stopped being distinguishable.\n\n### Step 2 Preflight — preflight the *data*, not only the environment\n\nA green test suite says the code runs; it says nothing about whether the corpus can teach the task. Adds assertions that **can fail**: per-label support split governance vs coding, every required slice existing as a *measured count*, token length against `--max-len`, and what a trivial baseline scores.\n\nGrounded: skipping this cost a full day here. A taxonomy, extractor, corpus, JAX baseline and a complete MLX training port were built before anything measured the data. Three defects were latent from the first corpus build — zero abstention rows in **both** corpora against `doc/finetuning.md:22`, governance at 6.8% of rows while being the entire point of the model, and ~80% of every prompt being the same 44 embedded schemas.\n\n### Step 4 Campaign execution — compute the requirement before you allocate\n\n**Compute the resource requirement from the config and refuse your own run if it does not fit.** A batch-16 / seq-2048 run needed **~54 GB** of retained attention activations on a **24 GB** host. It took the machine down — a reboot, not an OOM. The arithmetic takes ten seconds.\n\nAlso codified: framework memory caps are **advisory** (measured — a step peaked at 13.4 GB against a 12 GB cap and allocated straight through without raising); logs go somewhere that survives a restart (`/private/tmp` is wiped on reboot, which cost ~1.5 h of baseline logs); commit before launching; watch a **PID**, not a pattern; and a GPU job **looks idle** — 30% CPU / 960 MB RSS versus the JAX baseline's 600% / 8.7 GB.\n\n### Step 5 Verification — subgroup, same-sample baseline, null control\n\n- **Report the subgroup alongside the aggregate.** Aggregate top-3 of 47.00% looked like a pass while the governance split — the reason the model exists — sat at 19.1%, invisible at 6.8% of rows.\n- **Compare against a trivial baseline on the SAME rows.** 47.00% against a *quoted* 45.99% bar reads like clearing it; the same-sample static baseline was 46.70%, so the real margin was three rows in a thousand (z≈0.13). Comparing a measurement to a bar computed elsewhere manufactures a result. Run an untuned control too.\n- **Any correlation claim needs a null control** — this one is new and general. 68.8% of prompts followed by a commit within 15 minutes sounds decisive until shuffled timestamps score 30.3% from commit density alone. The finding is the **+38.5pp lift**. This is `AGENTS.md` §6's *\"a check that cannot fail is not a check\"* applied to statistics.\n\nRefs #1, #5, #7, #9.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated operational guidance for coordinating work across machines and branches.\n  * Added procedures for using GitHub issues and comments as the actionable record, including conflict resolution, evidence precedence, and decision tracking.\n  * Documented dataset checks, resource and restart-safety precautions, subgroup metrics, baseline comparisons, and null controls.\n  * Expanded anti-pattern guidance covering unsynchronized findings, ignored issue updates, and undocumented conflict resolution.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-09-08T16:23:22Z","updated_at":"2026-09-08T16:31:55Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"c1ebc966763ffe291b03b81cf68249795c4a8af9","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HiQS-Labs/Needle-fork/pulls/10/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HiQS-Labs/Needle-fork/pulls/10/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HiQS-Labs/Needle-fork/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HiQS-Labs/Needle-fork/issues/10/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.githu